BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:2026 Nova Institute for Health Media Fellowship
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260420T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260420T000000
UID:29e3a0c2086c63b557c6032f570b6d07@solutionsjournalism.org
DESCRIPTION:This opportunity is open to U.S. journalists.\nU.S. journalist
 s can now apply for the 2026 Nova Institute for Health Media Fellowship. T
 his program supports experienced print\, broadcast and digital journalists
  and nonprofit newsrooms reporting on the factors that affect health and w
 ell-being. It emphasizes complexity\, and solutions-focused work is defini
 tely welcome. The fellowship lasts for one year and comes with a $60\,000 
 award plus travel reimbursement. Applications close April 20.
LOCATION:This opportunity is open to U.S. journalists.
URL:https://novainstituteforhealth.org/our-communities/media-fellows/2026-
 media-fellowship-overview/
X-SOURCE:Solutions Journalism Network
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:⭐ APPLY NOW: Solutions Visuals - CBNI
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260424T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260424T000000
UID:62b5762d48c62d823ad63932f9332abe@solutionsjournalism.org
DESCRIPTION:This opportunity is open to newsrooms based in the United Stat
 es.\nThe Solutions Journalism Network is accepting applications for the se
 cond round of itsSolutions Visuals fellowship\, part of theClimate Beacon 
 Newsroom Initiative. While the story of climate change is often told throu
 gh images of natural disasters and environmental devastation\, this progra
 m supports newsrooms across the United States in developing innovative vis
 ual narratives that explore how communities are responding to the climate 
 crisis with evidence-based solutions. The first cohort\, launched in 2024\
 , produced visual storytelling on topics ranging from coastal restoration 
 and water conservation to flood resilience and Indigenous land management.
 \nThis year\, six newsrooms will be selected to receive $10\,000 each alon
 g with a year of coaching and support from SJN staff and partners\, includ
 ing award-winning photographers and visual storytellers. Proposals can foc
 us on any visual medium — photography\, video\, interactives\, illustrat
 ion or animation. Selected newsrooms will also have opportunities to exhib
 it their work in spring 2027 through partnerships withCatchLightandPhotovi
 lle.\nThe application deadline is Apr. 24. Join us for an informational 
 “Ask Me Anything” session about this programon Apr. 14.\nCatchLightis 
 a visual-first media organization that leverages the power of visual story
 telling to inform\, connect and transform communities. Its live event and 
 touring exhibition\, “CatchLight Live: Sharing What Matters\,” fosters
  community engagement in visual journalism\, inviting local audiences to c
 onnect with powerful storytelling\, share their perspectives and participa
 te in conversations that shape how their stories are seen and understood.\
 nPhotovilleis a New York-based nonprofit that works to promote a wider und
 erstanding of and increased access to the art of photography for all. It p
 roduces an annual citywide photography festival in New York\, a range of f
 ree educational initiatives and a nationwide pr
LOCATION:This opportunity is open to newsrooms based in the United States.
URL:https://solu.news/CBNI-2026
X-SOURCE:Solutions Journalism Network
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:When Everything Feels Urgent: How to Care for Yourself Anyway
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260428T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260428T000000
UID:1988666e8d07369429f65f8a50b62a36@solutionsjournalism.org
DESCRIPTION:Online\nHolly Wise is a journalist\, an educator\, a facilitat
 or and a former SJN-er. On April 28\, she'll host “When Everything Feels
  Urgent: How to Care for Yourself Anyway\,” a 45-minute online workshop 
 on “caring for yourself in the midst of urgency.” It promises to be a 
 space for a reset and a place to gain insight into practices that help you
  stay present when things are hard. It’s free to all.
LOCATION:Online
URL:https://www.linkedin.com/events/7442466116666535936/
X-SOURCE:Solutions Journalism Network
END:VEVENT
