BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:News Ambassadors' Depolarization Strategies Training
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260429T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260429T000000
UID:9f2724ef64507124e65f745ee6c1d133@solutionsjournalism.org
DESCRIPTION:Online\nAs a former SJN Complicating the Narratives Fellow and
  the director of News Ambassadors\, Shia Levitt is deeply committed to cre
 ating constructive\, solutions-focused reporting around even the most ince
 ndiary issues. While they usually offer depolarization training to newsroo
 ms\, classrooms and leadership cohorts\, Shia and News Ambassadors are hos
 ting a training on April 29 that is open to all. Donations are welcome\, a
 nd all go to News Ambassadors’ work. In the training\, you’ll learn te
 chniques for breaking binaries in your reporting\, listening differently a
 nd deeply\, fighting confirmation bias and more.
LOCATION:Online
URL:https://sojonewsambassadors.org/events/
X-SOURCE:Solutions Journalism Network
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Earth Journalism Network's Biodiversity Story Grants 2026
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260501T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260501T000000
UID:1fca36ba9b1da416a7219d51c9d8deb9@solutionsjournalism.org
DESCRIPTION:Earth Journalism Network is offering five to 10 grants for sto
 ries or projects that “raise global awareness about new threats or solut
 ions” around biodiversity. Journalists from any country may apply\, thou
 gh the stories should cover countries listed by the World Bank as low- or 
 middle-income. Explore the details\, and get your application in by May 1.
URL:https://earthjournalism.net/opportunities/biodiversity-story-grants-20
 26
X-SOURCE:Solutions Journalism Network
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Monthly Introduction to Solutions Journalism Webinar: May
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260505T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260505T000000
UID:622652596192812bc228c7cbbd8426d6@solutionsjournalism.org
DESCRIPTION:Online (Zoom)\nThis one-hour Solutions Journalism Network webi
 nar will explore the principles and pillars of solutions journalism. We wi
 ll discuss its importance\, outline key steps for reporting a solutions st
 ory\, and share tips and resources for journalists investigating responses
  to social problems. We will also introduce additional resources\, such as
  the Solutions Story Tracker\, a database with over 17\,000 stories tagged
  by beat\, publication\, author\, location and more\, along with a virtual
  heat map highlighting successful efforts worldwide.
LOCATION:Online (Zoom)
URL:https://us06web.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_9ykIGH3URYCXHGW7e5cmng
X-SOURCE:Solutions Journalism Network
END:VEVENT
